From ca7063fbff6c5f0e64301561285479a65ac334a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MacScope contributors <contributors@macscope.invalid>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 05:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(gst): harden external I/O readiness and lifecycle

Make an accepted zero-length feed wake the I/O thread so a host can signal output readiness after callback backpressure without injecting terminal bytes.

Check closure and mailbox capacity under the admission lock before copying, preserving bounded transient allocation and feed linearization. Add allocation-failure oracles, semantic style/mode chunk invariance, final-frame-before-close observation, the public surface-free registry race, and deadline-bound real-thread synchronization.

Keep all callbacks on the I/O thread and retain the existing bounded queue, byte-exact callback, resize, and terminal-state behavior.
